ason":null,"unit_id":"agent:E4","usage":{"input_tokens":150908,"output_tokens":3894,"requests":5}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.75,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Correct AC5 so the corruption also makes the stored `dir_mtime_ns` stale (or deletes/alters the mtime), since `_changed` skips any directory whose stored mtime matches the live mtime before the hash is consulted, so a hash-only corruption yields `indexed == 0`.","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.25,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["catchup.py:161-165 `_changed`: `if previous is not None and mtime_ns != UNKNOWN_MTIME and previous[0] == mtime_ns: continue` — a directory with an unchanged stored mtime is skipped and never hashed.","catchup.py:201-204 `_apply`: the `previous[1] != dir_hash` comparison that increments `indexed` only runs for directories `_changed` already returned, i.e. only those whose mtime moved.","Plan text: 'corrupting a stored `dirstate` hash and asserting the follow-up catch-up then reports `indexed > 0`' — a hash-only corruption leaves dir_mtime_ns matching, so the follow-up reports indexed == 0, the opposite of the AC's requirement."],"finding":"AC5's negative-control premise is refuted by the two-level diff: corrupting only a stored `dirstate` hash does not force a re-index, because `_changed` skips any directory whose stored mtime still matches the live mtime before the hash is ever consulted.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3457782479f4a74f","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance criteria, AC line: 'A test demonstrates the new invariant fails when it is violated, by corrupting a stored dirstate hash and asserting the follow-up catch-up then reports indexed > 0.'","norm_id":"n98637d6da3386f4d","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer writes the AC5 negative-control test exactly as specified (UPDATE dirstate SET dir_hash=... only), runs catch_up, and observes indexed == 0; the test meant to prove the invariant can fail instead proves nothing, or is silently 'fixed' by weakening the assertion."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Reword AC5 to corrupt both columns, e.g. 'by setting a stored `dirstate` row's `dir_mtime_ns` stale AND its `dir_hash` to a wrong value, so `_changed` re-hashes the directory and `_apply` finds the stored hash mismatched, and asserting the follow-up catch-up then reports `indexed > 0`.'","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Specify in the negative-test AC that the corruption must leave the corrupted directory in the `changed` set (e.g. also perturb its stored mtime, or run the follow-up as the guaranteed lag run immediately after a rebuild) so indexed>0 is actually reachable.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["catchup.py:161-166 `_changed` skips any dir whose stored mtime equals the live mtime (`previous[0] == mtime_